lled um  living towards eternal life saint  anselm's christian anthropology  i also gave a paper at the wisdom  conference  in wisconsin back in my home state  viterbo university up in la crosse  i gave a paper on human and divine  wisdom and anselm of canterbury  uh again which i haven't done anything  with i suppose i i really ought to  then uh 2012 once i'd moved up here to  new york i gave a paper  at the felician ethics conference um  what kind of moral theory does saint  anselm actually hold  another paper i still have to do  something with i've promised it to their  their journal actually but i haven't  revised it the way i ought to  and what was kind of interesting is is  that trip down there to felicia  which is in new jersey coincided with  going further down into new jersey  because my wife and i were invited by  saint anselm parish  to go as guests and give a dinner  address  and so i did a little talk about who is  saint anselm because  um you know they found out about me  through my internet article  uh you know the the internet  encyclopedia philosophy  entry on saint anselm which by the way  is  you know if you put it into like a paper  format it's like  um 50 pages long that's a that's a  pretty deep  long article  so anyway that was kind of fun i got to  meet a lot of nice people who were quite  interested in anselm  we were going to do some talks but then  of course um  uh you know the hurricane hit and kind  of put the kibosh on that and they've  been doing some rebuilding but  eventually  i think we'll probably do that and then  i recently gave a paper  well two papers um this year in 2013  one was in in april and it was at  another you know conference at  franciscan university steubenville uh  that was oriented around the question  must morality be grounded upon god and  so i gave a paper called an encelamian  grounding of morality  where i said yeah for anselm more or  less and here's how it would play itself  out  that paper i'm actually revi